WEBVTT

00:00:06.236 --> 00:00:08.656
<v><b>Friend:</b></v> What was your best ever New Year’s Eve?

00:00:09.237 --> 00:00:10.941
One you always remember?

00:00:11.623 --> 00:00:15.654
<v><b>Denisa:</b></v> Oh, definitely 2014, when I was in Rio.

00:00:15.907 --> 00:00:16.669
<v><b>Friend:</b></v> Who were you with?

00:00:17.232 --> 00:00:20.872
<v><b>Denisa:</b></v> I was with my boyfriend Marcelo, who’s Brazilian.

00:00:21.465 --> 00:00:22.776
<v><b>Friend:</b></v> Why was it so special?

00:00:23.116 --> 00:00:29.192
<v><b>Denisa:</b></v> Well, Brazil has special traditions for New Year’s Eve, and they were all new for me.

00:00:29.437 --> 00:00:34.044
For example, it’s a Brazilian tradition to wear white clothes for New Year’s Eve

00:00:34.759 --> 00:00:37.383
because white is a symbol of peace,

00:00:38.303 --> 00:00:42.591
so I wore a beautiful white dress that Marcelo’s mother bought me.

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:45.636
I have a photo somewhere on my phone.

00:00:49.059 --> 00:00:50.555
Yes, here, look!

00:00:51.005 --> 00:00:53.871
<v><b>Friend:</b></v> How pretty. So, what did you do?

00:00:54.615 --> 00:00:56.575
<v><b>Denisa:</b></v> Uh, let me think.

00:00:57.286 --> 00:01:02.187
Well, first we had a typical New Year’s Eve dinner with Marcelo’s family.

00:01:02.946 --> 00:01:08.450
And then, I guess it was about ten, we got a bus to Copacabana.

00:01:09.171 --> 00:01:11.184
<v><b>Friend:</b></v> What was the atmosphere like there?

00:01:11.532 --> 00:01:16.245
<v><b>Denisa:</b></v> Oh, it was amazing! The streets were already full of people.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:22.853
We went to a show at a place near the beach. It was great, and we danced the samba.

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.308
<v><b>Friend:</b></v> Wow. Were you there at midnight?

00:01:26.739 --> 00:01:30.027
<v><b>Denisa:</b></v> No, no. When we saw it was almost midnight,

00:01:30.052 --> 00:01:33.257
we went to the beach, and the typical countdown started,

00:01:33.282 --> 00:01:37.423
you know – ten, nine, eight…Happy New Year!

00:01:38.361 --> 00:01:41.926
Everywhere we heard the sound of people celebrating,

00:01:42.218 --> 00:01:45.205
and we watched the wonderful fireworks.

00:01:45.755 --> 00:01:50.404
<v><b>Friend:</b></v> It sounds great. What did people do when the fireworks finished?

00:01:50.762 --> 00:01:53.480
<v><b>Denisa:</b></v> Most people went to other parties, or they went home.

00:01:53.804 --> 00:01:54.851
<v><b>Friend:</b></v> And what about you?

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:57.752
<v><b>Denisa:</b></v> We decided to go to a different beach,

00:01:57.941 --> 00:02:03.462
a beach called Praia do Arpoador, and we took our first swim of the new year.

00:02:04.365 --> 00:02:05.452
It was magical.